<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:27:53 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>科学家发现大脑变化可以预测未来的痴呆症</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/scientists-find-brain-change-that-may-predict-future-dementia</link><description>这一发现暗示了一种更早发现风险的新方法，但科学家警告说，这远非最终的测试。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-find-brain-change-that-may-predict-future-dementia.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:27:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/scientists-find-brain-change-that-may-predict-future-dementia</guid></item><item><title>AI 观察 AI：加州大学洛杉矶分校系统捕获的数字病理学中的危险错误</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/ai-watching-ai-dangerous-errors-in-digital-pathology-caught-by-ucla-system</link><description>研究简介：加州大学洛杉矶分校研究人员创建的一种基于人工智能的工具，在检测潜在的危及生命的错误（称为现实幻觉）时，准确率高达 99.8%，这种错误偶尔来自虚拟染色人工智能模型。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/ai-watching-ai-dangerous-errors-in-digital-pathology-caught-by-ucla-system.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:12:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/ai-watching-ai-dangerous-errors-in-digital-pathology-caught-by-ucla-system</guid></item><item><title>一种新型艾滋病毒药物刚刚通过人体首次测试</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/a-new-kind-of-hiv-pill-just-passed-its-first-test-in-humans</link><description>科学家刚刚公布了第一批结果&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/a-new-kind-of-hiv-pill-just-passed-its-first-test-in-humans2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:57:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/a-new-kind-of-hiv-pill-just-passed-its-first-test-in-humans</guid></item><item><title>这种氨基酸可以帮助身体对抗肿瘤和病毒感染</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/this-amino-acid-may-help-the-body-fight-tumors-and-viral-infections</link><description>氨基酸精氨酸有助于保持人体运转，最显着的是通过合成执行一系列细胞过程的蛋白质。它由我们的身体产生，存在于常见的高蛋白食物中。精氨酸水平低与许多疾病有关，包括结肠癌。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/this-amino-acid-may-help-the-body-fight-tumors-and-viral-infections.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:42:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/this-amino-acid-may-help-the-body-fight-tumors-and-viral-infections</guid></item><item><title>量子随机性帮助神经网络识别麻烦的手写数字</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/quantum-randomness-helps-neural-network-recognize-troublesome-handwritten-digits</link><description>量子计算和人工智能是发展最快的现代技术之一。几十年来，人工智能以机器学习的形式被用于推荐电影和电视节目，并使图像搜索变得更加容易。在过去的几年里，大型语言模型已经渗透到日常生活的更多方面，从编写电子邮件到根据几行文字表达的请求生成图像、视频和歌曲。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/quantum-randomness-helps-neural-network-recognize-troublesome-handwritten-digits.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:27:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/quantum-randomness-helps-neural-network-recognize-troublesome-handwritten-digits</guid></item><item><title>心脏的“小大脑”如何帮助其发挥功能并保护其免受压力</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/how-the-hearts-little-brain-helps-it-function-and-protects-it-against-stress</link><description>多年来，科学家们已经知道心脏有自己的神经网络，即内在心脏神经系统（ICNS），有时被称为“小大脑”。它到底是如何运作的仍然是个谜，但一篇新论文&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/how-the-hearts-little-brain-helps-it-function-and-protects-it-against-stress2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 12:12:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/how-the-hearts-little-brain-helps-it-function-and-protects-it-against-stress</guid></item><item><title>颠倒研讨会以恢复科学论文遗漏的内容</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/inverting-the-seminar-to-recover-what-scientific-papers-leave-out</link><description>一篇科学论文读起来就像是从问题到结果的一个清晰的过程。然而，研究几乎从来不会以这种方式进行。实验失败了，对话改变了项目的方向，但这些都没有被印刷出来。当某个领域的创始人退休时，他们的隐性知识也随之消失，没有任何记录表明它的存在。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/inverting-the-seminar-to-recover-what-scientific-papers-leave-out2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:57:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/inverting-the-seminar-to-recover-what-scientific-papers-leave-out</guid></item><item><title>新的超声技术突破血脑屏障治疗神经胶质瘤</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/new-ultrasound-technique-breaches-blood-brain-barrier-to-treat-gliomas</link><description>UVA Health 研究人员确定，被称为神经胶质瘤的肿瘤可能比正常脑组织更容易接受靶向药物输送，这是聚焦声波改善脑肿瘤护理潜力的一个有希望的迹象。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-ultrasound-technique-breaches-blood-brain-barrier-to-treat-gliomas2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:42:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/new-ultrasound-technique-breaches-blood-brain-barrier-to-treat-gliomas</guid></item><item><title>用 CAR 细胞疗法重置自身免疫性疾病</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/resetting-autoimmune-disease-with-car-cell-therapies</link><description>致病性 B 细胞激活是许多自身免疫性疾病 (AID) 的基础，消除 B 细胞是一种颇具吸引力的治疗方法。表达嵌合抗原受体 (CAR) 的细胞最初被开发并成功用于治疗某些癌症，现在越来越多地被开发用于选择性消耗 B 细胞并“重置”艾滋病患者的免疫系统。在这篇综述中，我们调查了这个快速发展的领域，提供了有关当前艾滋病治疗中未满足的需求以及 CAR T 细胞如何满足这些需求的见解。特别是，我们探讨了深度 B 细胞耗竭的概念，讨论了当前可用的技术并回顾了与艾滋病治疗相关的关键靶标（CD19 和 B 细胞成熟抗原）。我们总结了有关自体和同种异体 CAR T 细胞在这种情况下的功效、安全性、风险和局限性的当前证据。最后，我们从技术和临床的角度讨论了针对艾滋病的工程化 CAR 表达细胞疗法的开发的未来前景。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/resetting-autoimmune-disease-with-car-cell-therapies.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:27:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/resetting-autoimmune-disease-with-car-cell-therapies</guid></item><item><title>30 年研究发现中风中种族和社会经济不平等现象日益扩大</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/widening-ethnic-and-socioeconomic-inequalities-in-stroke-identified-in-30-year-research</link><description>&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/widening-ethnic-and-socioeconomic-inequalities-in-stroke-identified-in-30-year-research2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:12:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/07/widening-ethnic-and-socioeconomic-inequalities-in-stroke-identified-in-30-year-research</guid></item></channel></rss>